{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1554228-few-questions-about-changelings-arts-and-treasures","id":1554228,"title":"Few questions about changelings, arts and treasures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-07T11:37:58-07:00","id":1554228,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Few questions about changelings, arts and treasures","content":"Generic question:<br /> Redcap abilities mention being able to intimidate anything at -2 difficulty. Even things that would usually be impossible to. How far does that goes? Like can you intimidate a locked door into opening? or something like that. Asking because otherwise it is already possible to intimidate ghosts, spirits, animals, etc.<br /> Huakai Po get 1 automatic success per scene on anything. Does that mean they can do something like read a book in foreign language they do not actually know?<br /> Elongated tongue merit gives you 2 feet long tongue. Do mortals see it? do they feel it if licked from impossible distance? Also, I guess it doesn't inconvenience the character in speaking and such unlike similar fomori power?<br /> Can you combine 2 arts in same cantrip?<br /> <br /> Questions about Arts:<br /> Autumn Eyes - description doesn't mention required Realms. I assume the realm determines what can be scrutinized? Makes it quite lopsided.<br /> The Poisoned Apple - could you poison wind using Nature realm? Would it then affect the first living thing in it's path, or a whole group?<br /> Set in Stone - if used on fire in conjunction with Nature, would that mean the fire keeps burning without fuel and keeps damaging?<br /> Deja Wu - not sure how it works. So for example, a redcap with Unforgettable taste can take a bite out of someone, go back in time and now they have the taste added to the memories? Or for example, can they grab a blade and send it back in time to themselves? Temporis+Prop<br /> Time Dilation - if used on oneself, would it create the Time Stop phenomenon? Can the character interact with world like that? Because Mage game has wristwatch that does exactly that. Also, provided example (rotting/aging staff) is pretty much the same as Autumn. I think more interesting example is given in Exalt books, like shooting an arrow into the future. So you shoot a bullet and choose target/time of who is stuck later.<br /> Burning Thew - Can you combine self buff with weapon buff? Like Dragon's Ire+Fae and Dragon's Ire+Prop or Nature.<br /> Holly Strike - does good enough damage (though only lethal). But what happens if you aim it something stranger? for example Dragon's Ire+Prop - would it strip target of all arms/armor/cloths but leave them unharmed? What about Dragon's Ire+Nature? Like can you erase swath of air? sorta like improvised vacuum bomb.<br /> Worms and Giants - how big/small can you get without unleashing? Do you have to spend glamour with each casting? How big/small could you get with Unleashing? Also, combining with other realms lets you do some interesting things. Like for example, if you could shrink a watermelon and make someone swallow it (or several) whole. Or put some shrunk stones in their pockets. Or shrink their cloth/jewelry while they are wearing it.<br /> <br /> Questions about Treasures:<br /> Invisibility hat - if we are using hat enchanted by Chicanery 2: Wailed eyes - how would you determine the duration of effect? One minute per glamour? One hour?<br /> Little hat of nightmares - enchanted with Legerdemain 3: Effigy to retrieve things/beings from there. I was thinking to add limitation of it being only scary or creepy things. What should the level of such an item be?<br /> Armored jacket - if enchanted both with Dragon's Ire 2 and 3 (+2 on hit and damage difficulties), what would be the rating?<br /> Belt of Giants - A belt that allows wearer to change size. How big drastic should the size change be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T14:58:16-07:00","id":1554431,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Redcap abilities mention being able to intimidate anything at -2 difficulty. Even things that would usually be impossible to. How far does that goes? Like can you intimidate a locked door into opening?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> That's the overall idea.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that Changeling powers come from the Dreaming, which is a reality of stories and narrative logic. That means even within the setting the &quot;physics&quot; behind them aren't based on cause-effect, but on drama and rule-of-cool.<br /> <br /> In short, the specifics of the effect are up to the ST. The Redcap can Intimidate inanimate objects and even ideas, but the result is whatever the ST thinks it should be at the moment and don't have to be consistent.<br /> <br /> Most of the time, thought, that's exactly the goal: you Intimidate an object into working and it complies. You can &quot;convince&quot; a device that's struggling to work into working smoothly, or you can convince a switch-like device (like a lock) into switching state. Anything more complex is up to the ST if it work at all and at which difficulty and number of successes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Huakai Po get 1 automatic success per scene on anything. Does that mean they can do something like read a book in foreign language they do not actually know?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Yes and no, but mostly no.<br /> <br /> This Birthright does not guarantees you can make the roll in the first place, and it doesn't change how the roll works. First you declare the action as normal. <u><b>IF</b></u> the ST calls for a roll, <i>then</i> you can declare the use of this Birthright, or not. If you can't try without it, you can't try with it.<br /> <br /> Also, some actions require more successes, you can't simply declare the result you want out of a single success. If you can roll to read this book, then the Birthright may apply, but the ST still decides the result based on successes and that's only a single guaranteed success.<br /> <br /> Still, not only does a number of rolls benefit from every single extra success, there are many simple but extraordinary actions with high difficulties (even 9 or 10) where this Birthright can have impressive, if not preternaturally looking, results. Or even preternaturally looking, since you can use it on Cantrips and other supernatural feats.<br /> <br /> Overall this is an extremely useful Birthright due to its flexibility.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Elongated tongue merit gives you 2 feet long tongue. Do mortals see it? do they feel it if licked from impossible distance? Also, I guess it doesn't inconvenience the character in speaking and such unlike similar fomori power?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Unless a Merit specifies that it only affects your <i>fae mien</i>, or otherwise states its effects are Chimerical, they're completely material aspects of your character and humans will notice and react accordingly. You're probably better hiding this tongue.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Can you combine 2 arts in same cantrip?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> AFAIR, no.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Autumn Eyes - description doesn't mention required Realms.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> No Art does that, because it's always up to you.<br /> <br /> It's not lopsided, it's how Cantrips work. You can always combine an Art with any and all Realms you want to design an effect.<br /> <br /> A rather famous combination is Hopscotch + Prop + Scene to make a building jump.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Poisoned Apple - could you poison wind using Nature realm? Would it then affect the first living thing in it's path, or a whole group?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> No reason not to work, although the details are up to the ST.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Invisibility hat - if we are using hat enchanted by Chicanery 2: Wailed eyes - how would you determine the duration of effect? One minute per glamour? One hour?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Usually, however long you keep the hat on.<br /> <br /> Treasures aren't meant to be hard or costly to use, they're already rather limited by Cantrip standards. Any limitation is completely up to the ST, as is actually any aspect of the treasure working at all.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Little hat of nightmares - enchanted with Legerdemain 3: Effigy to retrieve things/beings from there. I was thinking to add limitation of it being only scary or creepy things. What should the level of such an item be?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> 3.<br /> <br /> Limitations are already expected for a Treasure, they don't affect their level. A Treasure that access the whole scope of what an Art can do at a given level is what should be weird and rare.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Armored jacket - if enchanted both with Dragon's Ire 2 and 3 (+2 on hit and damage difficulties), what would be the rating?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Probably 5, if it's even possible, although nothing stops the ST from lowering it to 4 or 3 if they think the result isn't all that powerful.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T10:25:17-08:00","id":1554973,"title":"","content":"First of all - thanks for answers!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keep in mind that Changeling powers come from the Dreaming, which is a reality of stories and narrative logic. That means even within the setting the &quot;physics&quot; behind them aren't based on cause-effect, but on drama and rule-of-cool.<br /> <br /> In short, the specifics of the effect are up to the ST. The Redcap can Intimidate inanimate objects and even ideas, but the result is whatever the ST thinks it should be at the moment and don't have to be consistent.<br /> <br /> Most of the time, thought, that's exactly the goal: you Intimidate an object into working and it complies. You can &quot;convince&quot; a device that's struggling to work into working smoothly, or you can convince a switch-like device (like a lock) into switching state. Anything more complex is up to the ST if it work at all and at which difficulty and number of successes. </div> </div> </div>It's not that. Even beyond that one could assume you are just intimidating spirit of the item. It is just not clear what is meant when book says &quot;intimidate anything&quot;. Like, does it mean it should be something the fae could already socially interact with, or goes beyond that. But if it's accepted that anything can be intimidated as long as it's IC - all clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, some actions require more successes, you can't simply declare the result you want out of a single success. If you can roll to read this book, then the Birthright may apply, but the ST still decides the result based on successes and that's only a single guaranteed success.<br /> <br /> Still, not only does a number of rolls benefit from every single extra success, there are many simple but extraordinary actions with high difficulties (even 9 or 10) where this Birthright can have impressive, if not preternaturally looking, results. Or even preternaturally looking, since you can use it on Cantrips and other supernatural feats. </div> </div> </div>Same case here. But I guess you can only add the success to roll if you can make a roll. It is very useful, especially if combined with Jack-of-All-Trades and/or Self-Confident<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless a Merit specifies that it only affects your <i>fae mien</i>, or otherwise states its effects are Chimerical, they're completely material aspects of your character and humans will notice and react accordingly. You're probably better hiding this tongue. </div> </div> </div>As it was in section about supernatural merits I sorta assumed it was part of a mien. So Stone Skin is also visible?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not lopsided, it's how Cantrips work. </div> </div> </div>I meant you only need Fae 1 or 2 to use it in combat vs changelings, but would need quite high in actor to use vs humans.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A rather famous combination is Hopscotch + Prop + Scene to make a building jump.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I am myself fond of using wayfare+nature+time to ride around on boulders like the first pioneers. XD<br /> <br /> and one more thing about treasures. If I want to have a sort of a living treasure. Like lets say a hat that is at the same time actually a living insecty thing only pretending to be a hat. So it can jump off and scurry around on it's own. How should that be statted out as a treasure, or a chimera? \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T00:16:00-08:00","id":1555005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that. Even beyond that one could assume you are just intimidating spirit of the item. It is just not clear what is meant when book says &quot;intimidate anything&quot;. Like, does it mean it should be something the fae could already socially interact with, or goes beyond that. But if it's accepted that anything can be intimidated as long as it's IC - all clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not intimidating a spirit. Anything means anything.<br /> <br /> It is <u><b>meant</b></u> to not make sense. That's Changeling for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I guess you can only add the success to roll if you can make a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> The Birthright doesn't change the circumstances in which a roll happens, it only adds a success. For that to work, a roll must happen in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Stone Skin is also visible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it isn't made of stone, read the description. <b>Stone Skin</b> only makes your skin thicker.<br /> <br /> But yes, it's measurably thicker than normal, if it somehow comes to that.<br /> <br /> There's also <b>Granite Skin</b> that do, indeed, make your skin into stone, but only affects your <i>Fae Mien</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant you only need Fae 1 or 2 to use it in combat vs changelings, but would need quite high in actor to use vs humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still normal for any Art.<br /> <br /> You can use it on Gallain, you can use it on any person, you <u><b>can</b></u> use it on objects or animals.<br /> <br /> Every Art can be coupled with every Realm. Some combinations are more or less obvious, but mentioning required Realms is not a thing.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How should that be statted out as a treasure, or a chimera?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it's animation is either natural or the direct effect of the Art within, this would be a Chimera.<br /> <br /> Treasures are a <b>special</b> kind of magical item. Most interesting things in Changeling are actually Chimeras, not Treasures, even magical items.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}